    ('economic-development', 2, 'Gustafson''s documented economic-development record is entirely small-business and downtown centered: a former downtown small-business owner herself (Bella Donna''s Bistro & Patisserie on 21st Street), her October 2020 candidate Q&A proposed increased city financial support for downtown businesses, emergency business plans, subsidies for businesses offering Pacific University student discounts, and closer city-university collaboration, while her 2024 reelection platform lists "Downtown revitalization" and "Small Business Stability" as priorities and her October 2024 Q&A named downtown revitalization through supporting small businesses a top funding priority. As City Club of Forest Grove president she works on community revitalization outreach, per her official city bio. Nothing in her record involves recruiting major employers with tax abatements; this matches the small-business-support-and-local-entrepreneur-programs chair.', ARRAY['https://forestgrovenewstimes.com/2020/10/26/forest-grove-city-council-candidates-field-questions/', 'https://forestgrovenewstimes.com/2024/09/20/donna-gustafson-seeks-reelection-to-forest-grove-city-council/', 'https://www.forestgrove-or.gov/611/Meet-the-Council']::text[]),
